Round 1 (two independent reviewers at high, on main..c63e0b7): one on
correctness, one told to attack the game-thread/render-thread synchronisation.
8 + 6 findings.

  HIGH, and the one that mattered: the round-1 fix for MEDIUM-1 hosted the
  capture in dds_Unlock's DDSCAPS_PRIMARYSURFACE branch, which is gated on
  g_ddraw.render.run -- cleared by the WINDOW thread on deactivate, minimise,
  fullscreen toggle and mode change -- and is reached only on the flip's
  DirectDraw arm at 0x4C6475, never the GDI BitBlt arm at 0x4C63C0. An arm
  could wait for an arbitrary later frame, answer with an unrelated picture
  stamped with the wrong time, or never be serviced. The safety argument had
  become a fix by timing. Fixed by servicing the arm on the trigger family's
  NEXT pass instead.

  Also acted on: tascene ab's retired glshot call; the same-second filename
  collision that ate an arm; write_ddraw_ini still writing openglcore; stale
  render_ogl.c comments; the glshot --help text.

  REJECTED with evidence: that gl_draws is true during Vulkan bring-up.
  tagpu_vk_own_present() is render_vk.c:145, above the frame loop at :154 that
  holds the only surviving tagpu_overlay_draw at :232.

  CORRECTED IN MY OWN DOCS: the reason after_flip is unusable is not an
  s_opsLive test inside it (it has none) but that tagpu_detour_observe emits
  test eax,eax; jz and hijacks the return only when before_flip returns
  non-zero, and before_flip returns 0 at if (!s_opsLive).

